-- title:
--   A uniform space envelope for local-parameter construction
-- statement:
--   Let $h,w\in\mathbb N$, where $h$ is the local half-size parameter and $w$ is the workspace's starting address. Let $S_{\mathrm{params}}(w,h)$ be the declared space limit for the concrete procedure that constructs local graph counts, selects the prime, and computes the bucket cap. Then
--
--   $$
--   S_{\mathrm{params}}(w,h)\le w+2^{2048(h+1)+2}.
--   $$
--
--   The space limit is an address bound, so the additive $w$ accounts for the placement of the workspace. No positive lower bound on $h$ is assumed.
--
--   This estimate puts the parameter-construction workspace under the same elementary envelope used to absorb local work into the eventual global resource budget.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LocalParameterBounds.lean#L150-L177

